🔥 Final Module 1.3 Mastery Test

After studying everything, you should be able to answer without notes:

Round 1 — Fundamentals

Class vs object

State vs behavior

Object vs reference

Encapsulation

Constructor

this

inheritance

polymorphism

abstraction

interface

composition


Round 2 — Output

Predict code involving:

constructors

this()

super()

overriding

overloading

dynamic dispatch

field hiding

static method hiding

interface defaults

casting


Round 3 — Internals

Explain:

object creation

reference semantics

runtime type

dynamic dispatch

compile-time overload resolution

runtime overriding

JVM/JIT considerations


Round 4 — Debugging

Given broken Java code:

identify → explain → fix → justify.

Round 5 — Design

Given a real requirement:

choose between

class / interface / abstract class / inheritance / composition

and explain why.

Round 6 — Production

Design the payment system from scratch, including replaceable providers, composition, abstractions, validation, immutability, failure handling and future extensibility—the same production-style target specified by your module. 


---

✅ Completion standard

Don't consider 1.3 complete just because you can define OOP terms.

You should reach:

Explain → Implement → Predict → Debug → Explain internals → Handle edge cases → Refactor → Discuss trade-offs → Design production system → Answer senior interview questions.

That matches the module's own final mastery gate, including dynamic dispatch, field/static hiding, interfaces, abstract classes, composition, LSP, JVM behavior, performance and production trade-offs. 
